Architecture decision (inline page, not surface composition):
  The shell registers pages via a parameterless ctor and does NOT inject the data layer (IApiClient /
  CacheThenNetworkEngine / IWidgetVehicleSource) into pages — confirmed in ShellWindow.xaml.cs. Every done page
  (RegenEfficiencyPage, BatteryHealthPage, …) is therefore a SELF-CONTAINED inline renderer over its own feed
  (Empty default + a .Create(IApiClient, vehicleId, …) DI-host entry), fully unit-testable via a mock feed. Pages
  and surfaces are independent parity units (RegenEfficiencyWidget and RegenEfficiencyPage both exist, each with a
  full implementation). This page reproduces all 11 web regions inline in that same convention rather than composing
  the pre-built FeatureViews.Driving surfaces (which would require data-layer wiring the page does not receive).

Files:
  feature-views/DrivingDynamicsPage/DrivingDynamicsPage.Model.cs       (7 tolerant JSON parsers: MotorReading,
      DriveRow, DriveDynamicsReading, AutopilotReading, CoachData, MotorStats(computeMotorStats) + snapshot + feed + EmptyFeed + state enum)
  feature-views/DrivingDynamicsPage/DrivingDynamicsPage.Display.cs     (all 11 region display records + DrivingDynamicsDisplay + DrivingDynamicsModel)
  feature-views/DrivingDynamicsPage/DrivingDynamicsPage.Projection.cs  (pure projection of all 11 regions + Registration + Diagnostics)
  feature-views/DrivingDynamicsPage/DrivingDynamicsPage.Source.cs      (DrivingDynamicsClientFeed — generated C# client, 7 reads)
  feature-views/DrivingDynamicsPage/DrivingDynamicsPage.ViewModel.cs   (INotifyPropertyChanged holder, loading/error/success + freshness + date range)
  feature-views/DrivingDynamicsPage/DrivingDynamicsPage.cs             (WinUI 3 UserControl, Fluent + design tokens, all 11 regions)
  TeslaSync.App.Tests/FeatureViews/DrivingDynamicsPageTests.cs         (37 headless tests)
  TeslaSync.App.Tests/TeslaSync.App.Tests.csproj                       (link the 5 UI-free files; the WinUI view is build-only)

Data sources (P1/S8 INotifyPropertyChanged VM → generated C# client, web hook names kept at the C# call sites):
  useMotorLatest          -> ApiRequest("get_api_v1_motor_latest", Query{vehicle_id})            — PRIMARY (gates loading→success, web motorLoading)
  useMotorHistory         -> ApiRequest("get_api_v1_motor", Query{vehicle_id, limit})            — best-effort
  useDrives               -> ApiRequest("get_api_v1_drives", Query{vehicle_id})                  — best-effort
  useDrivingCoach         -> ApiRequest("get_api_v1_analytics_driving_coach", Query{vehicle_id}) — best-effort
  useDriveDynamicsLatest  -> ApiRequest("get_api_v1_drive_dynamics_latest", Query{vehicle_id})   — GForce + Pedal children (best-effort)
  useVehicleState         -> ApiRequest("get_api_v1_vehicles_vehicleID_state", Path{vehicleID})  — Autopilot child (best-effort)
  useSignalObservations   -> ApiRequest("get_api_v1_signals_observations", Query{vehicle_id, field, limit}) — Autopilot cruise/follow (best-effort)
  Failure semantics: the primary motor read propagates ApiException (page error surface); every other read is
  independently fault-tolerant (BestEffortAsync) — mirroring the web's separate React-Query hooks.
Units (P1/S5): SI read from the API; converted only at the display boundary in DrivingDynamicsProjection via
  UnitFormatters.FormatTemperature/FormatSpeed/FormatDistance + UnitConverters.SpeedFromSi/TemperatureFromSi +
  ScalarFormatters (power_kw/regen_kw/torque/RPM are rendered verbatim with their unit suffix, exactly as web).
Live data: the web children use polling React-Query (refetchInterval), not useLiveX/SSE; the page VM exposes a
  TsDataFreshness chip (UpdatedAt/IsFetching/IsError). No SSE subscription required (ADR-013 staleness n/a here).

